(ra-review
  "docs/coherence-substrate/form-neutral-language-world-model.md"
  "Second independent implementation audit; do not edit any file. The first round returned REVISE because selected-field accounting omitted faithful/provenance/recipe descendants, malformed anchor/alignment categories could enter fnwm-extend, and the prose named wm-observe one step too high. Read model/form-neutral-language-world-model.fk, model/tests/form-neutral-language-world-model-band.fk, cognition/core-frequency-lift-form-neutral-crossing.fk, cognition/core-frequency-lift-dictionary.fk, form/form-stdlib/world-model.fk, model/concept-world-model.fk, and form/form-stdlib/dsv4-token-recipe-swap.fk. Freshly preflight and run the integration band plus the dictionary, crossing, world-model, and concept-world-model bands. Try to break the repair rather than accepting its description: construct direct graphs whose only differences are faithful surface length, provenance descendants, and shallow versus deep numeric recipes; verify every reachable string and cell changes the recomputed envelope, a tight budget admits the smaller and rejects the larger, excessive walk depth rests outside, and callers cannot attest a smaller size. Offer shaped but wrong-category anchors and alignments, zero alignment residue, negative ordinal, overflow anchor, mismatched anchor, and unknown top-level category; they must rest as absence without changing the prior graph. Recheck bidirectional provenance-preserving mapping query, directed candidate relations, semantic render closure, generic wm-entity-embed/persist/orient use, held-open novelty, idempotent extension, and the DS4-specific—not universal LLM—comparison. Distinguish observed integration from open semantics, cultural review, shard policy, tokenizer IDs, generation, and scale performance. Return PASS AS A BOUNDED WORLD-MODEL INTEGRATION, REVISE, or BLOCK with located executable evidence. Agreement without pressure probes is not useful.")
